  "articleBody": "After a hailstorm, you might be looking at your roof and wondering if those little dings are just superficial or if they're a sign of something much more serious. It's a common question, and understanding the difference between cosmetic and functional damage is key to making the right decisions about repairs. What looks like a minor flaw could hide a significant problem.\n\n**What Can Change the Right Choice**\nCosmetic damage typically affects the appearance of your roof without compromising its ability to protect your home. Think minor dents in metal flashing or gutters that don't impair their function, or very light granule loss on shingles that isn't widespread. These issues don't immediately threaten the integrity of your roof or lead to leaks. Functional or structural damage, on the other hand, directly impacts the roof's ability to shed water and protect your home. This includes fractured shingles, significant granule loss exposing the asphalt, torn or bruised membranes, or deeply dented metal components that create low points where water can pool. These types of damage can shorten your roof's lifespan dramatically and eventually lead to leaks. The tricky part is that some cosmetic damage can become functional over time, especially in Texas where intense sun and seasonal storms can worsen initial impacts. A qualified professional can differentiate between these types of damage and advise you on the best course of action.\n\n**When Professional Guidance Helps**\nWhile some signs might seem obvious, it's really hard for an untrained eye to tell the difference, especially with small or subtle impacts. A professional inspection can accurately assess the extent of the damage, identifying if impacts have shortened the roof's service life or compromised its weather resistance. They'll provide a detailed report, often with photos, clearly distinguishing between observed damage and their professional opinion. This is crucial for insurance claims, as what's covered can vary based on whether the damage is deemed cosmetic or functional. Discounted Roofing Co. specializes in storm damage assessments and can give you an honest evaluation.\n\n**What to Do Next**\nIf you're unsure whether your roof's hail damage is cosmetic or functional, don't guess. Contact Discounted Roofing Co. for a comprehensive hail damage inspection. We'll help you understand exactly what your roof needs to stay protective for years to come.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-03"
}